uld be included, only the tasks.\n\nPutting it all together, I'll structure each task with the correct module, parameters, and any conditions. I'll ensure the YAML is properly formatted without any comments or explanations, just the tasks as required.\n\nFinally, I'll start the playbook with '---' followed by the tasks in the specified order. I'll double-check each task to make sure I haven't missed any parameters or conditions. This should result in a valid Ansible Playbook that fits into an Ansible Role under tasks/main.yml.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install epel\n  ansible.builtin.epel:\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install epel gpg key\n  ansible.builtin.rpm_key:\n    key: https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/RPM-GPG-KEY-EPEL-2\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install epel-release\n  ansible.builtin.yum:\n    name: epel-release\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install epel-next-release\n  ansible.builtin.yum:\n    name: epel-next-release\n    state: present\n    when: epel_next | default('false') == 'true'\n  notify: update_package_cache\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T08:13:14.581899428Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12459732902, 'load_duration': 89506423, 'prompt_eval_count': 383, 'prompt_eval_duration': 90472085, 'eval_count': 718, 'eval_duration': 12278236351, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--129c642f-e7ca-4acb-a275-240675309321-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 383, 'output_tokens': 718, 'total_tokens': 1101}
