les, set owner and group.\n\nTask 11: Copy Vault binary. Use the copy module to move the binary from download path to the destination. Set mode=0755 and notify the handler \'Restart vault\'.\n\nTask 12: Set capability cap_ipc_lock=ep. The set_cap module is used here. I need to set the capability on the binary without marking the task as changed, so changed_when=false.\n\nTask 13: Touch vault.env. Using the file module with state=touch to create the file if it doesn\'t exist. Set the correct owner and group.\n\nTask 14: Create /usr/lib/systemd/system directory. Use file module with path and state=directory.\n\nTask 15: Copy service file. Use copy module to move the template to the destination. Notify \'Daemon reload\' only if the service manager is systemd. I\'ll need to check the platform, maybe using ansible_distribution.\n\nTask 16: Copy vault configuration. Use copy module to move vault.hcl to the correct path, set mode and notify \'Restart vault\'.\n\nTask 17: Flush handlers. Use the meta module with flush_handlers.\n\nI need to ensure that each task uses the correct modules and variables as specified. Also, the playbook should start with \'---\' and be valid YAML without any extra comments or explanations.\n\nI should make sure that all the variables like {{ vault_group }}, {{ vault_user }}, etc., are properly defined elsewhere, but in the playbook, I just use them as is.\n\nI also need to make sure that the tasks are in the correct order, as specified, and that each one is a valid YAML task entry. No hosts or vars sections since this is part of an Ansible Role\'s tasks.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now I\'ll structure each task with the correct module and parameters.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create Vault group\n  group:\n    name: "{{ vault_group }}"\n\n- name: Create Vault user\n  user:\n    name: "{{ vault_user }}"\n    home: "{{ vault_user_home }}"\n    shell: "{{ vault_user_shell }}"\n    group: "{{ vault_group }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Create Vault download directory\n  file:\n    path: "{{ vault_download_path }}"\n    state: directory\n    owner: "{{ vault_user }}"\n    group: "{{ vault_group }}"\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Download Vault binary\n  get_url:\n    url: "{{ vault_binary_url }}"\n    dest: "{{ vault_download_path }}/vault.tar.gz"\n\n- name: Extract Vault binary\n  unarchive:\n    src: "{{ vault_download_path }}/vault.tar.gz"\n    dest: "{{ vault_download_path }}"\n    mode: gzip\n\n- name: Set owner to root for Vault binary\n  file:\n    path: "{{ vault_download_path }}/vault"\n    owner: root\n\n- name: Check if vault_path exists\n  stat:\n    path: "{{ vault_path }}"\n\n- name: Create vault_path if it does not exist\n  file:\n    path: "{{ vault_path }}"\n    state: directory\n    owner: "{{ vault_user }}"\n    group: "{{ vault_group }}"\n    mode: 0755\n  when: not vault_path_exists\n\n- name: Create directories in vault_path\n  file:\n    path: "{{ item }}"\n    state: directory\n    owner: "{{ vault_user }}"\n    group: "{{ vault_group }}"\n    mode: 0755\n  loop: "{{ vault_directories }}"\n\n- name: Create data directory\n  file:\n    path: "{{ item }}"\n    state: directory\n    owner: "{{ vault_user }}"\n    group: "{{ vault_group }}"\n    mode: 0755\n  loop: "{{ vault_data_directories }}"\n\n- name: Generate TLS key and certificate\n  openssl_genpkey:\n    genkey: true\n    algorithm: rsa\n    rsa_bits: 4096\n    keyout: "{{ vault_data_directory }}/tls/vault.key"\n    days: 1095\n    nocert: false\n    req:\n      common_name: "Vault Server"\n  register: tls_key\n  notify: Restart vault\n\n- name: Generate TLS certificate\n  openssl_req:\n    key: "{{ vault_data_directory }}/tls/vault.key"\n    out: "{{ vault_data_directory }}/tls/vault.pem"\n    subject: "CN=Vault Server"\n    x509_extensions: v3_ca\n  notify: Restart vault\n\n- name: Set ownership of TLS files\n  file:\n    path: "{{ item }}"\n    owner: "{{ vault_user }}"\n    group: "{{ vault_group }}"\n  loop: "{{ vault_tls_files }}"\n\n- name: Copy Vault binary\n  copy:\n    src: "{{ vault_download_path }}/vault"\n    dest: "{{ vault_path }}/usr/bin/vault"\n    mode: 0755\n  notify: Restart vault\n\n- name: Set cap_ipc_lock=ep on /usr/bin/vault\n  set_cap:\n    path: /usr/bin/vault\n    capability: ipc_lock\n    state: ep\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Touch vault.env\n  file:\n    path: "{{ vault_path }}/etc/vault.d/vault.env"\n    state: touch\n    owner: "{{ vault_user }}"\n    group: "{{ vault_group }}"\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: Restart vault\n\n- name: Create /usr/lib/systemd/system directory\n  file:\n    path: /usr/lib/systemd/system\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Copy Vault service file\n  copy:\n    src: vault.service.j2\n    dest: /usr/lib/systemd/system/vault.service\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: Daemon reload\n  when: ansible_distribution == "CentOS" or ansible_distribution == "Fedora" or ansible_distribution == "RedHat"\n\n- name: Copy vault configuration\n  copy:\n    src: vault.hcl\n    dest: "{{ vault_path }}/etc/vault.d/vault.hcl"\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: Restart vault\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta:\n    flush_handlers: yes\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T08:15:21.954904446Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 35236137405, 'load_duration': 86102132, 'prompt_eval_count': 999, 'prompt_eval_duration': 384821189, 'eval_count': 1756, 'eval_duration': 34763830682, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--0cbf74c4-d568-4350-9817-472d23fb8732-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 999, 'output_tokens': 1756, 'total_tokens': 2755}
