s_family in ["RedHat", "Debian"]\n\nWhich is 69 characters. Also under 80.\n\nBut perhaps other tasks have longer lines. For example, the \'Install Docker packages\' task has a \'yum\' and \'apt\' block, which might be long.\n\nWait, looking at the original, task 4 has:\n\n- name: Install Docker packages\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ docker_packages }}"\n    state: "{{ docker_packages_state }}"\n    become: yes\n  yum:\n    name: "{{ docker_packages }}"\n    state: "{{ docker_packages_state }}"\n    become: yes\n  when:ansible_version < "2.12" or ansible_os_family in ["RedHat", "Debian"]\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\nThis is a single task with multiple modules. But the \'when\' is correctly placed under the task.\n\nWait, perhaps the issue is that the \'when\' is part of the task and not the module. So the \'when\' applies to the entire task, which includes both apt and yum. So, the structure is correct.\n\nBut the user\'s error messages only point to specific lines, so I\'ll focus on those.\n\nIn summary, the main issues are:\n\n1. Missing space after colon in \'when\' conditions, causing truthy value errors.\n2. Syntax error due to missing colon in \'when\' condition.\n3. Line length issues on lines 50 and 93.\n\nTo fix:\n\n- Add space after colon in \'when\' conditions.\n- Split long \'when\' conditions into multiple lines using lists for better readability and to comply with line length.\n- Ensure that each \'when\' condition is properly indented and formatted.\n\nNow, I\'ll reconstruct the playbook with these fixes.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Load OS-specific vars\n  include_vars:\n    file: "{{ ansible_os_family }}.yaml"\n    ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Include RedHat-specific setup tasks\n  include_tasks: setup-RedHat.yml\n  when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat"\n\n- name: Include Debian-specific setup tasks\n  include_tasks: setup-Debian.yml\n  when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n\n- name: Install Docker packages\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ docker_packages }}"\n    state: "{{ docker_packages_state }}"\n    become: yes\n  yum:\n    name: "{{ docker_packages }}"\n    state: "{{ docker_packages_state }}"\n    become: yes\n  when:\n    - ansible_version < "2.12"\n    - ansible_os_family in ["RedHat", "Debian"]\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Install Docker packages (with downgrade option)\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ docker_packages }}"\n    state: "{{ docker_packages_state }}"\n    version: "{{ docker_packages_version | default(\'\') }}"\n    become: yes\n  yum:\n    name: "{{ docker_packages }}"\n    state: "{{ docker_packages_state }}"\n    version: "{{ docker_packages_version | default(\'\') }}"\n    become: yes\n  when:\n    - ansible_version >= "2.12"\n    - ansible_os_family in ["RedHat", "Debian"]\n\n- name: Install docker-compose plugin\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: docker-compose --version || true\n    changed_when: false\n  when:\n    - docker_install_compose_plugin\n    - ansible_version < "2.12"\n    - ansible_os_family not in ["RedHat", "Debian"]\n\n- name: Install docker-compose-plugin (with downgrade option)\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: docker-compose --version || true\n    changed_when: false\n  when:\n    - docker_install_compose_plugin\n    - ansible_version >= "2.12"\n    - ansible_os_family in ["RedHat", "Debian"]\n\n- name: Ensure /etc/docker/ directory exists\n  file:\n    path: /etc/docker\n    state: directory\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0755\n  when: docker_daemon_options is defined\n\n- name: Configure Docker daemon options\n  copy:\n    content: "{{ docker_daemon_options | to_yaml }}"\n    dest: /etc/docker/daemon.json\n    mode: 0644\n  when: docker_daemon_options is defined\n  notify: restart docker\n\n- name: Ensure Docker is started and enabled at boot\n  systemd:\n    name: docker\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n  when:\n    - docker_service_state\n    - docker_service_enabled\n  ignore_errors: yes\n\n- name: Ensure handlers are notified now to avoid firewall conflicts\n  ansible.builtin.meta:\n    flush_handlers: yes\n\n- name: Include docker-compose.yml tasks\n  include_tasks: docker-compose.yml\n  when: docker_install_compose\n\n- name: Get docker group info using getent\n  getent:\n    db: group\n    key: docker\n    fields: all\n\n- name: Check if there are any users to add to the docker group\n  set_fact:\n    users_to_add: "{{ users_in_docker_group | default([]) | difference(upstream_users_in_docker_group | default([])) }}"\n\n- name: Include docker-users.yml tasks\n  include_tasks: docker-users.yml\n  when: users_to_add | length > 0\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T08:48:20.268710737Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 119238592845, 'load_duration': 92534023, 'prompt_eval_count': 1833, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1096388596, 'eval_count': 4984, 'eval_duration': 118048173004, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--e3b6cb8e-dab1-4c17-85e0-5f09f76dcd01-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1833, 'output_tokens': 4984, 'total_tokens': 6817}
