ned. Using the template module to write to /etc/pip.conf. I\'ll set the state to present to ensure the line is added.\n\nTask 8: Set trusted hosts. Similar to Task 7, using template to add the trusted_host lines.\n\nTask 9: Update pip if certain conditions are met. Use pip module with state=latest, but only if python_pip_update is true and the OS isn\'t bookworm, noble, or Alpine. I\'ll need to use the when condition with ansible_os_family and not in [\'Debian\', \'Alpine\'].\n\nTask 10: Install requested modules if OS is not bookworm, noble, or Alpine. Again, using pip module to install from requirements, but only if the OS conditions are met.\n\nI also need to ensure that the tasks are in the correct order, as specified. Each task should be a separate entry in the playbook, with the correct module and arguments.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with the appropriate module, path, state, and conditions where necessary. For tasks that depend on variables, I\'ll include the when clauses as needed.\n\nLet me make sure all paths are correctly specified and that variables are properly referenced. Also, I\'ll use the correct module names, like ansible.builtin.file and ansible.builtin.pip, to ensure compatibility.\n\nFinally, I\'ll compile the entire playbook, ensuring that it starts with \'---\' and is a valid YAML file. I\'ll double-check each task to make sure there are no typos or syntax errors.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if python3.11 EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file exists\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /path/to/python3.11/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    state: exists\n\n- name: Rename python3.11 EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file if it exists\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /path/to/python3.11/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    state: renamed\n    new_path: /path/to/python3.11/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED.old\n\n- name: Check if python3.12 EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file exists\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /path/to/python3.12/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    state: exists\n\n- name: Rename python3.12 EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file if it exists\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /path/to/python3.12/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    state: renamed\n    new_path: /path/to/python3.12/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED.old\n\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  ansible.builtin.import_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n  args:\n    host: localhost\n\n- name: Install python pip\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: python3-pip\n    state: present\n\n- name: Configure pip proxy\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    dest: /etc/pip.conf\n    mode: 0644\n    content: |\n      proxy = {{ python_pip_proxy }}\n    state: present\n\n- name: Trust hosts\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    dest: /etc/pip.conf\n    mode: 0644\n    content: |\n      trusted-host = {{ python_pip_trusted_host }}\n    state: present\n\n- name: Update pip\n  ansible.builtin.pip:\n    name: pip\n    state: latest\n    when:\n      - python_pip_update\n      - ansible_os_family not in [\'Debian\', \'Alpine\']\n\n- name: Install requested modules\n  ansible.builtin.pip:\n    requirements: "{{ python_pip_modules }}"\n    state: present\n    when:\n      - ansible_os_family not in [\'Debian\', \'Alpine\']\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T09:12:19.753050121Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 25756395870, 'load_duration': 87504740, 'prompt_eval_count': 638, 'prompt_eval_duration': 351406610, 'eval_count': 1263, 'eval_duration': 25316732200, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--ab25d30f-2eab-484d-898b-78d8c84aed15-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 638, 'output_tokens': 1263, 'total_tokens': 1901}
