ould remove the \'state\' parameter or set it to \'present\' if that\'s sufficient.\n\nAnother issue is the \'file\' module tasks not having \'owner\' and \'group\' specified, but in the faulty playbook, they do have \'owner: root\' and \'group: root\', so perhaps the problem is elsewhere. Maybe the \'file\' module is not the right choice for renaming, and \'rename\' module should be used instead.\n\nSo, for tasks 2 and 4, I\'ll replace the \'file\' module with \'ansible.builtin.rename\' module. This way, we can correctly rename the files without using an invalid \'state\' parameter.\n\nFor the \'pip\' tasks, I\'ll remove the \'state: latest\' to avoid the warning, or set it to \'present\' if that\'s acceptable. Alternatively, since we\'re updating pip, maybe the \'version\' isn\'t necessary, but the \'when\' condition is correctly used.\n\nLet me go through each task:\n\n1. Task 1 and 3 are using \'file\' with \'state: file\' which is correct. No issues here.\n\n2. Task 2 and 4 are using \'file\' with \'state: renamed\', which is wrong. I\'ll change these to use the \'rename\' module.\n\n3. Task 5 is importing tasks, which seems fine.\n\n4. Task 6 installs pip, which is correct.\n\n5. Tasks 7 and 8 use \'template\' to configure pip.conf. They have \'owner\' and \'group\' set, so that\'s okay.\n\n6. Task 9 uses \'pip\' with \'state: latest\' and \'when\'. I\'ll remove \'state\' or set it to \'present\' to fix the linting issue.\n\n7. Task 10 uses \'pip\' with \'requirements\' and \'when\'. Again, \'state: present\' is correct, so I\'ll keep that.\n\nNow, I\'ll structure the corrected playbook with these changes, ensuring that all tasks are in order and only the necessary fixes are applied without altering the original task sequence or functionality.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if python3.11 EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file exists\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /path/to/python3.11/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    state: file\n\n- name: Rename python3.11 EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file if it exists\n  ansible.builtin.rename:\n    path: /path/to/python3.11/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    new_path: /path/to/python3.11/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED.old\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n\n- name: Check if python3.12 EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file exists\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /path/to/python3.12/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    state: file\n\n- name: Rename python3.12 EXTERNALLY-MANAGED file if it exists\n  ansible.builtin.rename:\n    path: /path/to/python3.12/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED\n    new_path: /path/to/python3.12/EXTERNALLY-MANAGED.old\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  ansible.builtin.import_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n  args:\n    host: localhost\n\n- name: Install python pip\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: python3-pip\n    state: present\n\n- name: Configure pip proxy\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    dest: /etc/pip.conf\n    mode: \'0644\'\n    content: |\n      proxy = {{ python_pip_proxy }}\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n\n- name: Trust hosts\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    dest: /etc/pip.conf\n    mode: \'0644\'\n    content: |\n      trusted-host = {{ python_pip_trusted_host }}\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n\n- name: Update pip\n  ansible.builtin.pip:\n    name: pip\n    state: present\n    when:\n      - python_pip_update\n      - ansible_os_family not in [\'Debian\', \'Alpine\']\n\n- name: Install requested modules\n  ansible.builtin.pip:\n    requirements: "{{ python_pip_modules }}"\n    state: present\n    when:\n      - ansible_os_family not in [\'Debian\', \'Alpine\']\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T09:13:43.527597333Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 33758971730, 'load_duration': 93847616, 'prompt_eval_count': 3040, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1543714704, 'eval_count': 1410, 'eval_duration': 32119925433, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--909a19ea-4e42-4162-9d7b-653d1c674e09-0' usage_metadata={'input_token