_requirements and openssl_pip_packages should be defined elsewhere since they\'re not specified here.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with the appropriate module, command, and variables. Also, for the shell commands, I\'ll set changed_when=false to indicate it\'s just a check.\n\nNow, putting it all together in YAML, making sure each task is correctly indented and follows the syntax. I\'ll start with \'---\' and then list each task under a \'tasks\' key.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if python is installed\n  shell: which python\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Check if python3 is installed\n  shell: which python3\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Debug Python executable path\n  debug:\n    msg: "Python executable path: {{ lookup(\'pipe\', \'which python\') }}"\n\n- name: Debug Python3 executable path\n  debug:\n    msg: "Python3 executable path: {{ lookup(\'pipe\', \'which python3\') }}"\n\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Install requirements\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n  loop: "{{ openssl_requirements }}"\n\n- name: Ensure packaging is available via dnf\n  dnf:\n    name: python3-packaging\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install pip packages\n  pip:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: latest\n  loop: "{{ openssl_pip_packages }}"\n\n- name: Create key directory\n  file:\n    path: "{{ key_dir }}"\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n    owner: root\n\n- name: Create csr directory\n  file:\n    path: "{{ csr_dir }}"\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n    owner: root\n\n- name: Create crt directory\n  file:\n    path: "{{ crt_dir }}"\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n    owner: root\n\n- name: Include create.yml\n  import_tasks: create.yml\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T09:59:33.525655407Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 20027441235, 'load_duration': 91210977, 'prompt_eval_count': 564, 'prompt_eval_