ow is set. I\'ll use template module with the file and state. The condition will check if users_cron_allow is defined.\n\nTask 7 ensures /etc/cron.allow doesn\'t exist if users_cron_allow isn\'t set. I\'ll use file module with state=absent and the condition.\n\nNow, I\'ll structure each task with the correct module, arguments, and conditions. I\'ll make sure each task is properly indented and in the correct order.\n\nI also need to ensure that variables like users_requirements, users_groups, etc., are correctly referenced. Since these are variables passed into the role, I don\'t need to define them here.\n\nFinally, I\'ll compile all these tasks into a YAML playbook, making sure it starts with \'---\' and each task follows correctly. I\'ll double-check the syntax to avoid any YAML errors and ensure it\'s valid for an Ansible Role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Install required software\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ users_requirements }}"\n    state: present\n  when: users_requirements is not empty\n\n- name: Loop over users_groups\n  loop: "{{ users_groups }}"\n  include_tasks: group.yml\n  when: users_groups is defined\n\n- name: Ensure the /etc/sudoers.d directory is included\n  lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/sudoers\n    line: \'##includedir /etc/sudoers.d\'\n    state: block\n  when: users_sudo_includedir is defined\n\n- name: Loop over users\n  loop: "{{ users }}"\n  include_tasks: user.yml\n  when: users is defined\n\n- name: Manage cron permission\n  template:\n    src: cron.allow.j2\n    dest: /etc/cron.allow\n  when: users_cron_allow is defined\n\n- name: Check existence of /etc/cron.allow\n  file:\n    path: /etc/cron.allow\n    state: absent\n  when: users_cron_allow is not defined\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T10:00:58.095380221Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 15053417454, 'load_duration': 93175274, 'prompt_e