he template module and notify the handler, but only if the OS is either Debian or Suse.\n\nTask 10: Import directories.yml for defined directories. Use import_tasks with a condition on directories_defined.\n\nTask 11: Flush handlers to execute them after tasks. I\'ll use the meta module with flush_handlers set to True.\n\nTask 12: Remove default index.html if the variable is true. Use the file module with state=absent and the condition on httpd_remove_example.\n\nTask 13: Start and enable httpd service. Use the service module with the specified service variable and ensure it\'s enabled.\n\nI also need to make sure that each task is in the correct order as per the instructions. No additional tasks should be added or omitted. The variables used in each task are important, so I\'ll ensure they\'re correctly referenced.\n\nSince the playbook is to be included in an Ansible Role under tasks/main.yml, I won\'t include any playbook-level headers like hosts or vars. Each task should be a valid entry in the playbook.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with the appropriate module, arguments, and any conditions or notifications. Proper indentation and YAML syntax are crucial to prevent errors.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the entire playbook to ensure all tasks are present, in the right order, and that the YAML is correctly formatted without any syntax issues.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Task 1: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  hosts: localhost\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Task 2: Install apache httpd\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ httpd_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Task 3: Configure selinux\n  selinux:\n    booleans: "{{ selinuxBOOLEANS }}"\n    ports: "{{ custom_PORTS }}"\n\n- name: Task 4: Configure httpd\n  template:\n    src: "{{ httpd_CONFIG_SRC }}"\n    dest: "{{ httpd_CONFIG_DEST }}"\n    group: "{{ httpd_CONFIG_GROUP }}"\n    mode: "{{ httpd_CONFIG_MODE }}"\n  notify: test_and_reload_httpd\n\n- name: Task 5: Activate httpd module | Debian\n  command: a2enmod "{{ item }}"\n  with_items: "{{ httpd_MODULES }}"\n  notify: test_and_reload_httpd\n  when: debian_system\n\n- name: Task 6: Import ssl.yml\n  import_tasks: ssl.yml\n  when: https_ENABLED\n\n- name: Task 7: Import locations.yml\n  import_tasks: locations.yml\n  when: locations_DEFINED\n\n- name: Task 8: Import vhosts.yml\n  import_tasks: vhosts.yml\n  when: vhosts_DEFINED\n\n- name: Task 9: Configure ports\n  template:\n    src: "{{ ports_CONFIG_SRC }}"\n    dest: "{{ ports_CONFIG_DEST }}"\n    group: "{{ ports_CONFIG_GROUP }}"\n    mode: "{{ ports_CONFIG_MODE }}"\n  notify: test_and_reload_httpd\n  when: (ansible_distribution == "Debian" or ansible_distribution == "Suse")\n\n- name: Task 10: Import directories.yml\n  import_tasks: directories.yml\n  when: directories_DEFINED\n\n- name: Task 11: Flush handlers\n  meta: flush_handlers\n\n- name: Task 12: Removing default html\n  file:\n    path: "{{ httpd_DEFAULT_INDEX }}"\n    state: absent\n  when: httpd_remove_example\n\n- name: Task 13: Start and enable httpd\n  service:\n    name: "{{ httpd_SERVICE }}"\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T10:10:26.125496516Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 25765004254, 'load_duration': 103364492, 'prompt_eval_count': 655, 'prompt_eval_duration': 413795409, 'eval_count': 1184, 'eval_duration': 25246753397, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--35d66778-e9f4-4766-898a-0545e649c165-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 655, 'output_tokens': 1184, 'total_tokens': 1839}
