content='<think>\nOkay, I need to fix the Ansible playbook so that it passes ansible-lint. Let me look at the error messages to understand what\'s wrong.\n\nFirst, the errors mention using FQCN for certain modules. I remember that FQCN stands for Fully Qualified Class Name, which means using the full path for modules like `ansible.builtin.import_tasks` instead of just `import_tasks`.\n\nLooking at the playbook, the first task uses `import_tasks: assert.yml`. I should change this to `ansible.builtin.import_tasks` to fix that linting issue.\n\nNext, the `apt` module is used, but the error suggests using `ansible.builtin.apt`. So I\'ll update that task to use the FQCN.\n\nThen, there\'s a task using `shell`. The error says to use `ansible.builtin.shell` instead. So I\'ll adjust that module call.\n\nThe `template` module also has the same issue, so I\'ll change it to `ansible.builtin.template`.\n\nAnother error is about using `shell` when `command` is sufficient. The task that runs `php --ini` can be replaced with the `command` module since it doesn\'t require shell functionality. This will also fix the idempotency issue because `command` is idempotent.\n\nThere\'s a warning about file permissions in the template task. I should set `chmod` to \'0o644\' to ensure proper file permissions, making it less risky.\n\nI\'ll make sure all other parts of the playbook remain unchanged, keeping the same task names, variables, and order. Only the necessary fixes for the linting issues will be applied.\n\nLet me go through each task step by step to apply these changes:\n\n1. **Import assert.yml**: Change to `ansible.builtin.import_tasks`.\n2. **Install php**: Update to `ansible.builtin.apt`.\n3. **Find used php.ini**: Replace `shell` with `command` and adjust the module parameters.\n4. **Configure php**: Use `ansible.builtin.template` and set `chmod`.\n\nI\'ll ensure the playbook starts with `---` and each task is correctly formatted. No other tasks or variables should be altered. This should resolve all the linting errors without changing the intended functionality.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  ansible.builtin.import_tasks: assert.yml\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Install php\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: "{{ php_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Find used php.ini\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: php --ini\n    register: php_found_ini_location\n    when: php_ini_location is not defined\n\n- name: Configure php\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: php.ini.j2\n    dest: "{{ php_ini_location | default(php_found_ini_location.stdout) }}"\n    notify: httpd_restart\n  changed_when: false\n  ignore_errors: true\n  register: php_configured\n\n- name: Set php.ini permissions\n  file:\n    path: "{{ php_ini_location | default(php_found_ini_location.stdout) }}"\n    state: file\n    mode: \'0o644\'' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T10:30:45.41969371Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14796622724, 'load_duration': 93913573, 'prompt_eval_count': 2321, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1257850197, 'eval_count': 662, 'eval_duration': 13442484424, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--da4f8c0a-e74c-464e-8cc3-f8f270b5af3c-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2321, 'output_tokens': 662, 'total_tokens': 2983}
