ther the variable `ansible_package_state` is correctly used. In the original, it\'s set as `state: "{{ ansible_package_state }}"`. I should ensure that the variable is properly defined elsewhere, but since the task description mentions it\'s dynamically set, I don\'t need to change that part.\n\nFinally, I\'ll structure the corrected playbook, ensuring it starts with \'---\' and each task is correctly indented and formatted in YAML. I won\'t add any extra tasks or modify the existing ones beyond what\'s necessary for linting fixes.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install Ansible\n  ansible.builtin.dnf:\n    name: ansible\n    state: "{{ ansible_package_state }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T11:45:22.046335203Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 10481196345, 'load_duration': 103986639, 'prompt_eval_count': 998, 'prompt_eval_duration': 345563682, 'eval_count': 590, 'eval_duration': 10030809844, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--d8e53576-c4a0-4509-8952-d0bf73c9a56a-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 998, 'output_tokens': 590, 'total_tokens': 1588}
