ariables as specified. Also, the order matters, so I\'ll follow the sequence given.\n\nI should also consider variables like rsyslog_features and rsyslog_deploy_default_config. They\'ll be defined elsewhere, so I don\'t need to set them here.\n\nPutting it all together, each task will be a YAML block under the main.yml file, starting with \'---\' and each task properly indented. I\'ll make sure there are no extra comments or explanations, just the tasks as specified.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now I\'ll structure the YAML accordingly, ensuring each task is correctly implemented.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Uninstall conflicting systemd-logger\n  apt:\n    name: systemd-logger\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Install rsyslog\n  apt:\n    name: rsyslog\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install additional rsyslog packages\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n    become: yes\n  loop: "{{ rsyslog_features }}"\n\n- name: Configuring default rsyslog\n  template:\n    src: default_config.j2\n    dest: /etc/rsyslog.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  when: rsyslog_deploy_default_config | default(true)\n  notify: restart rsyslog\n\n- name: Make configuration directory\n  file:\n    path: /etc/rsyslog.d/\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Configuring rsyslog forward rule\n  template:\n    src: forward_rule.j2\n    dest: /etc/rsyslog.d/forward.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  when: not rsyslog_deploy_default_config | default(true)\n  notify: restart rsyslog\n\n- name: Configuring additional config files\n  copy:\n    src: "{{ item }}"\n    dest: /etc/rsyslog.d/\n    remote_src: yes\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  loop: "{{ additional_config_files }}"\n\n- name: Start and enable rsyslog\n  service:\n    name: rsyslog\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', '