utting it all together, I\'ll structure the playbook with each task in order, ensuring the YAML is correctly formatted and adheres to the role structure.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_file:\n    file: files/assert.yml\n\n- name: Install required packages\n  package:\n    name: "{{ selinux_requirements }}"\n    state: present\n  notify: \'Gather facts after package installation\'\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta:\n    flush_handlers: yes\n\n- name: Configure selinux\n  block:\n    - name: Manage selinux\n      selinux:\n        state: "{{ selinux_state }}"\n        policy: "{{ selinux_policy }}"\n      notify: \'Reboot system after selinux changes\'\n\n    - name: Manage selinux booleans\n      seboolean:\n        name: "{{ item.name }}"\n        state: "{{ item.state }}"\n        persistent: yes\n      loop: "{{ selinux_booleans }}"\n      loop_control:\n        label: "{{ item.name }}"\n  when:\n    - selinux_enabled\n    - connection == \'ssh\'\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T12:03:00.51168536Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12259075470, 'load_duration': 80468283, 'prompt_eval_count': 504, 'prompt_eval_duration': 138063825, 'eval_count': 649, 'eval_duration': 12039554892, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--e0c64391-7744-4d3a-9657-09fcdbc2aa13-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 504, 'output_tokens': 649, 'total_tokens': 1153}
